WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:06.740
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week on
Game of Thrones so many sad things happened,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.730
this face was my face after it was all over.
They wanted to make us wait a week because

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.019
they wanted to give us a break between WTF
moments.

00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:19.029
Before we mentally unpack all of them quick
shoutout for the giveaway. Just as a way to

00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:22.679
say thank you to you guys for being so awesome
I'm giving away an amazon gift card to a random

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:25.050
subscriber in the comments. All you have to
do to participate is be a subscriber and leave

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:30.429
a comment. I'm also willing to send out digital
hugs after what happened.

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:34.660
So first let's do top 5 top WTF moments, then
I'll do my review and circle back around for

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.660
any major plot points we need to remember.
Careful for spoilers if you haven't seen it

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.920
yet, here we go. Number 5 - Missendei and
Grey Worm 'shipping

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:49.770
This may have been one of the only happy moments
from the episode. The reason it's depressing

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:53.940
is because they'll never be able to consummate
their relationship. I'd argue that shouldn't

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.190
stop them from pursuing a companionship that
goes beyond simple friendship, it's just going

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.420
to make things really difficult.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.939
Based on the way they left things it seems
like Missandei wants to pursue something with

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:08.730
him, he's the one that seems reluctant. Given
enough time I think he'll come around.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:12.830
The thing that really struck me about them
is that of all the relationships we saw in

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:18.560
the episode, there's was the only one you
feel good about. Like Roose and Ramsay, Sansa

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.680
and Littlefinger. They just creep me out.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.890
Number 4 - Sansa Learns to Lie

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.890
Did you see how she died her hair black in
their last scene and they were giving each

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.940
other creepy looks. Big red flashing warning
lights going on everywhere. The whole Vale

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:38.940
story this week seemed more about Sansa shedding
most of her innocence, like she's slowly suffocating

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.370
the sweet summer child inside her.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.880
As pervy as Littlefinger seems with those
long gazes, his interest in her isn't just

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:50.740
sexual. It's more like he's taking pleasure
in watching her learn to play the game. I'm

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:53.380
really interested to see where they take Sansa's
character from here.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:57.060
It seems like by the end of this season, the
show will have caught up with book Sansa.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:02.880
Like when we get to Season 5, for her, the
show will be ahead of the books.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.560
Number 3 - Ser Jorah is Exiled

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.610
Poor Ser Jorah, he brought it on himself.
That external shot of the city when he was

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:14.349
riding out of town was so sad. It looked like
it was straight out of a really depressing

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:18.740
western movie. It almost made things worse
that Daenerys didn't scream at him. Like the

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:23.010
moment was so upsetting that she was just
screaming internally. Just like all of us

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.770
were screaming internally watching the episode.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:31.910
What I was confused by was the royal pardon.
He clearly got a copy of it way back in season

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:36.940
1. So was this a new copy? The seal of the
hand of the king was on it. So I'm assuming

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.700
what Jorah said was correct, Tywin Lannister
was trying to divide Daenerys inner circle

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.760
to keep them busy.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.590
I really hope Jorah isn't gone for the rest
of the season. But it seems like based on

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.020
the pacing of the story he'll be on Daenerys
shit list for the rest of this season. So

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.459
if we do see him he'll be on his own somewhere.

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:56.020
Number 2 - Ramsay Snow Becomes Ramsay Bolton

00:02:56.020 --> 00:03:00.530
This was one of the most twisted victory moments
I've seen this season. Like when something

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:06.200
really awful gets celebrated like Dwarf Jousting
or when a villain wins a big victory like

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.890
the Red Wedding. The show even changes the
music to this really uncomfortable tune so

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.260
that internally you kind of know not to cheer.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:21.099
Real quick though, no judging, be honest.
Which of you guys cheered when Roose named

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:25.459
Ramsay Snow a Bolton? My brain kind of melted
a little when it happened.

00:03:25.459 --> 00:03:30.310
If there was any doubt that something terrible
just happened, there was that line from Ramsay

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.739
telling Reek he'd be giving him a bath later.
Yuck.

00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:38.280
That's the best word to describe that whole
part of the story. The flayed Iron Born man

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:44.120
is a visual metaphor for that. In fact, if
any of your friends ever asked you to explain

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:49.200
Ramsay just show them a screencap of this
flayed man. That will tell them everything

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.150
they need to know.

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.860
I had a hard time telling because the video
I was watching was low rez, but they were

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:59.069
marching toward Moat Cailin way off in the
distance. For a minute it made me think of

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:04.340
Winterfell, because Roose had just got done
making this huge speech about being the Warden

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:08.780
of the North but Winterfell is what you think
when you think of The North.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:13.900
and my Number 1 WTF moment, pretty easy to
guess Oberyn Martell VS The Mountain.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:18.329
So many things to unpack here. Let's start
with the fight itself. Pedro Pascal looked

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:22.510
like he was doing all the stunts. What they
did with the fight choreography was so much

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:27.370
better than what I had imagined. And even
though Oberyn got his skull crushed he in

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:33.380
fact did beat the Mountain. He just waited
too long to finish him off.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:37.680
That wicked looking pike of his was so awesome
too. Here's an up close shot of what the spear

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.990
tip looked like. He rammed that through the
Mountain's chest, severed his hamstring and

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.750
landed a few other deep slice cuts.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:48.780
I did a video kind of explaining the Mountain's
armor earlier today, when he's wearing it,

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:55.780
he's basically a walking fortress. So the
only way to land a blow was in the gaps between

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.080
plates. On the subject of armor too, even
if Oberyn had been wearing a helmet, the Mountain

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.470
still would have been able to crush his head
through it. So don't feel like ignoring Tyrion

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.440
had anything to do with him dying.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:11.370
I shouldn't have been surprised they showed
the wide shot of his body afterwards. Of all

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:16.280
the things the show has done on screen this
season I still think Joffrey's up close purple

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.910
face is worse.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:22.389
At the end of the season I'll do a breakdown
of all the most vomit inducing scenes. Like

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:25.530
a montage of WTF.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:29.110
For people that have read the books, please
don't go crazy with spoiler in the comments.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:36.110
The episode cut off right after the Mountain
collapsed. So he's still floating in the ether

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.820
even though he got the crap stabbed out of
him.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:43.590
This will go down as the best fight scene
the show has ever done to date. I challenge

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:49.009
the show runners to top it in a future season.

00:05:49.009 --> 00:05:54.000
But now it's your turn. Let me know what your
favorite moment was, and describe the face

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.580
you made when the Mountain squished Oberyn's
head.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:03.330
Overall I felt like this was a B plus episode
with an A plus fight attached at the end.

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:06.650
Usually the different scenes all over the
world connect on a really deep level, but

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:11.220
this week felt a little disconnected. In the
show's defense, that might have been the point.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:16.120
I think the secret to decoding the episode
is in decoding Orson Lannister. Smashing his

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:16.560
beetles.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:21.789
I paid special attention to Tyrion's speech,
it was incredibly long. And duration is a

00:06:21.789 --> 00:06:26.580
good indicator of how important the showrunners
think something is. Thus, listening to Tyrion

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.470
Decode Orson was one of the most important
things in the episode.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.620
I really think they were trying to convey
the idea of futility. Like no one understands

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.350
why they're killing all these people. The
beetles being a metaphor for the War of the

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.900
Five Kings and on a general level they just
represent any type of killing.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.650
That speech did not end on any kind of resolution.
They didn't answer the question about what

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:47.889
it all means. So I think we're headed for
a lot more senseless violence before the end

00:06:47.889 --> 00:06:50.550
of the season.
Let me know what you think the Beetle Speech

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.780
was about and what it means for the future.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:58.319
Really the only hanging threads at the end
of the episode are Tyrion and Arya. Tywin

00:06:58.319 --> 00:07:01.600
sentenced him to death, so we need to think
about what's going to happen to him in the

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.229
final two hours of the season. Please book
readers, if you're going to post spoilers

00:07:05.229 --> 00:07:09.759
be sure to use spoiler tags and just hit enter
four or five times before leaving a comment.

00:07:09.759 --> 00:07:15.889
As for Arya, I didn't put it in my Top 5 Moments,
but her reaction to her aunt dying was so

00:07:15.889 --> 00:07:19.910
awesome. I think she was laughing just because
it was just one more awful thing that could

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:24.490
have happened. It's like Murphy's Law. Anything
that can go wrong will go wrong. And she's

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:30.539
just laughing at the Universe. I like her
reaction better than Tyrion's reaction. I

00:07:30.539 --> 00:07:33.449
guess you could say he's subject to Murphy's
Law too.

00:07:33.449 --> 00:07:37.720
Right now the things I'm really looking forward
too is the Wildling Attack on the Night's

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:42.330
Watch, Arya and The Hound. There's really
only a couple more places for them to go.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:46.880
And finding out what the Martell's are going
to do once they learn Oberyn is dead.

